 "notes": "Approximate digitization; not supplied or endorsed by FUJIFILM. All page-3 charts are embedded raster images (no vector curve paths); characteristic curves were traced at native resolution from column-wise darkness peaks (columns on vertical grid lines and peaks on horizontal grid lines skipped and bridged), the spectral curve with a centreline follower after the 3 px grid lines were masked; axes calibrated on the printed grid lines. Characteristic curves (section 13): two charts, Microfine 20 C small-tank 5/10/15/20 min and D-76 20 C small-tank 4/7/10 min; all seven are in all_curves. channels.k is Microfine 10 min: the bulletin's own developer, the time its development table gives for EI 100 at 20 C (section 7), and the processing used for the published RMS granularity and resolving power. x is log H (lux-seconds) as charted. Where curves merge in the toe they are traced as one shared line; where they overlap into a single thick band (Microfine about log H -2.6 to -2.2, D-76 about -2.6 to -2.0) each curve is placed inside that band along a path interpolated between its resolved part and the shared toe, so it is uncertain by about the band half-width (about 0.01-0.02 D). Toe tracing noise (at most 0.009 D, D-76 4 min; under 0.001 D for Microfine) was removed with a running maximum so density is non-decreasing. log_h_ref: none. The charts carry no 18% grey, speed-point or normal-exposure mark; the text gives only ISO 100/21 and no grey-card density target, so no reference exposure is placed. Spectral sensitivity (section 14): 'Spectrogram to Daylight (5400K)', axis 'Relative Sensitivity (log)' with only a 1.0 log-unit bar between two grid lines; values are log10 relative sensitivity with 0 placed at the lower line of that bar (arbitrary common offset). The curve starts on the 400 nm grid line, which hides its first few nanometres; it is recorded from 403 nm. rms_granularity is the single printed Diffuse RMS Granularity Value (7; Microfine; 48 um aperture; sample density 1.0 above minimum density); no granularity curve is published. Not recorded (no field in this schema): time-G-bar curves (section 15), resolving power (60 lines/mm at 1.6:1, 200 lines/mm at 1000:1).",
